      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1799, settlers founded the first English school west of the Mississippi River at Mount Tabor in Cape Girardeau.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cape_Girardeau%2C_Missouri",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After the 1808 incorporation, Cape Girardeau evolved from a frontier trading hub into a bustling river port thanks to steamboats and railroads.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
